  "answers": [
    "Here's what deleting your local Google data would do. Nothing has been changed yet.\n\n**Actions that would run:**\n1. **Remove the locally stored Google tokens.** The app would no longer have local credentials for Google.\n2. **Cancel any active Google jobs** that are still running.\n3. **Permanently delete local Google records and retained raw responses.** This is the imported Google Health data stored on this computer.\n\n**What stays:**\n- **Takeout data is kept.** I set `include_takeout_data` to false, so any imported Google Takeout data is not touched.\n- **Remote authorization is not revoked.** The app stays authorized on your Google account. Deleting local data does not disconnect it at Google.\n- **Your Fitbit data is not affected**, since this only applies to the Google provider.\n\nThe deletion can't be undone. You'd need to re-import from Google to get the records back. The confirmation expires in 5 minutes.\n\nDo you want me to go ahead and delete the local Google data as described above? Reply yes to proceed, or no to cancel.",
    "The local Google API data has been deleted.\n\n- **Records deleted:** 3\n- **Raw files deleted:** 0\n- **Local Google tokens:** none were stored, so there were none to remove.\n- **Takeout data:** kept.\n- **Remote authorization:** not revoked, so the app is still authorized on your Google account.\n\nIf you want, I can check that the Takeout data is still there with `list_data_types`."
  ],
